  "instance_name": "onion_cutting_struggle",
  "label": "Onion Cutting Struggle",
  "description": "The concept of cutting onions causing tears is a common domestic experience rooted in real-world biology. Onions release sulfur compounds when cut, which react with enzymes to form syn-propanethial-S-oxide, a volatile gas that irritates the eyes and causes tears. This biological phenomenon is the basis for the meme's humor, as it is a relatable, non-dramatic physical discomfort. The meme relies on this real-world knowledge to create the analogy between physical pain and emotional discomfort.",
